# Taxonomie assets — règles normatives

Source canonique : `@ellipse/shared` → `src/assets/taxonomy.ts` et `pipeline-stages.ts`.

## 11 familles (ne jamais mélanger)

| Famille | Groupe | Rôles |
|---------|--------|-------|
| `heroes` | characters | hero |
| `companions_and_allies` | characters | companion, ally, guide, merchant, npc |
| `enemies` | characters | enemy, monster, summon, mount |
| `bosses` | characters | boss |
| `weapons_and_relics` | props | weapon, armor, relic |
| `interaction_props` | props | prop, checkpoint, door, portal, altar |
| `hazards_and_pickups` | props | hazard, trap, pickup, collectible |
| `biomes_and_maps` | environments | environment, biome, background, tileset |
| `ui_shells` | ui | ui |
| `sound_and_voice` | audio | music, sfx, voice |
| `fx_feedback` | fx | fx |

## Convention dossier

```
03_assets/<group>/<role>__<slug>/
  01_source/       # références verrouillées
  02_cutouts/      # segmentation alpha (SAM2, rembg)
  03_cleanup/      # découpe parts, nettoyage
  04_rig/          # rig 2D ou mesh 3D
  05_animation/    # motion packs, state machines
  06_exports/      # atlas runtime, manifests
  07_qa/           # gates qualité
  08_remote_jobs/  # work orders GPU
  pipeline.contract.json
  README.md
```

## Interdit

- Mélanger hero + enemy + boss dans un même dossier asset
- Stocker tileset et personnage dans `03_assets/characters/`
- Dupliquer labels familles/rôles dans Studio sans importer `shared`
- `family_id` incohérents entre `asset-taxonomy.json` et `model-routing.json`

## Agents par stage

| Stage | Agents runtime | Outils pipeline |
|-------|----------------|-----------------|
| 02_cutouts | character | SAM2, rembg, BiRefNet |
| 03_cleanup | character, decor | Sharp, Aseprite |
| 04_rig | animation, mesh_3d | 2D Pose Editor, Mixamo |
| 05_animation | animation | ComfyUI, Wan 2.x, ControlNet OpenPose |
| 06_exports | integration | Atlas JSON, glTF |
| 07_qa | qa | smoke bot, cutting QA |

